WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.680
Big Cleaning at the Café!

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.390
All times and places.

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:43.240
Year in, year out.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.400
What am I going to do?

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.540
The lightly salted salmon we got as a

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.170
year-end gift from Mrs. King Penguin

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.130
was a nice thought, 
but we don't eat salmon.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.680
Feature!

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.010
This Season's Must-Haves! 
Mix-and-Match Items

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.580
There you are, lazing 
around since morning.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.880
I can't clean with you there. 
You need to move.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.680
But I'm at a good part.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.070
If you're going to clean, do it outside.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.410
Don't suck me up!

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.470
Oh, my.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.530
Welcome.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.810
Hello.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.040
Jeez. My mom's so short-tempered, don't you think?

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.370
I don't think it's that 
your mom is short-tempered.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.940
I think you always say 
one thing too many.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.310
So she tried to suck you 
up with the vacuum again?

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.600
Apparently vacuums break easily.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:54.610
What? It broke?

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.630
Yeah! So she can't suck me up anymore!

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.280
I'll live happily ever after.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:01.600
I don't think that's the 
right phrase in this case.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.490
I'll give you one of these, Panda.

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.450
Polar Bear's Café Year-End Lottery

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.450
Everyone's a Winner

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.450
Lottery Ticket

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.450
Win Luxurious Prizes!!

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.450
Only Through 
December

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.450
What's that?

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.390
A ticket to be able to 
shake hands with me?

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.090
Yes!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.310
End of Line

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:14.630
Hand-shaking 
Event

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:14.240
It's a ticket for people to shake 
your hand at Polar Bear's Café.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.560
No, it's not.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.610
It's a lottery ticket for the drawing.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:21.050
We have luxurious prizes lined up.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.300
Luxurious prizes?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:28.520
Is this outfit necessary?

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.980
It's all about service, Miss Sasako.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.300
I mean, I'm not wearing 
this because I want to.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.030
No, I think you 
actually do want to.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:38.190
Nope.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.170
You're super excited to 
wear that, aren't you?

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.450
You've started butting
 into conversations, Miss Sasako.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.860
You've grown quite a bit this past year.

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:47.620
Pardon?

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.440
I don't think that growth 
is needed in the café.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.030
Let's get this lottery started!

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.480
Congratulations!

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.510
A big winner!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.520
Yay! Luxurious prizes!

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:16.040
Here you go. Your luxurious prize.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.190
A vacuum?

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.440
Congratulations!

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.910
A big winner!

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.510
Here you go. Your luxurious prize.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.330
A broom?

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:39.590
It's a high-quality item

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:42.080
that was hand-crafted 
by an artisan from a palm tree

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.430
I see...

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.300
Well, let's begin.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:46.760
Begin what?

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.390
The big cleaning.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.350
Really? Is that what this is about?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.270
It'll be fun if we all do it.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:56.970
You know, it's the end of the 
year, so I'm looking back...

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:00.160
But didn't I help you with 
weed pulling this past summer?

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.300
That might have happened.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:06.070
You don't see us as 
loyal customers, do you?

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:08.570
My loyal friends?

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.530
Just because you wrap things up well

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.440
doesn't mean you're forgiven.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:22.130
Don't suck me up!

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.090
What are you doing, Panda?!

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.050
There we go!

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:35.430
Don't suck me up!

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:40.440
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.520
A lottery?

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:45.870
Yes. Here you go.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.590
Congratulations!

00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.840
A big winner!

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.710
Big winner?

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.670
Silver 
Prize

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.670
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:03.200
Here you go, the silver prize.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.010
I wonder if it's a catalog 
for a trip to Hawaii.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.630
Ooh, what is it?

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:11.600
Food Coupon
All-You-Can-Eat Weeds
Polar Bear's Café

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.100
It's a food coupon.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.990
It's for all-you-can-eat weeds.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.730
That's great for Mr. Llama.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.440
Well then, Miss Sasako,

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.800
let's gather the things 
we don't need first.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:28.570
Yes.

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:31.320
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:36.830
Wow, there's a lot.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.750
Where did you even have this stuff?

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:41.590
Another Dimension Po—

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.910
It's not a good idea to do that joke!

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.920
What should I do with these?

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.650
You found some more things in the yard?

00:06:50.650 --> 00:06:51.760
That's amazing.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.290
You should probably 
have some professionals

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:57.240
conduct an archaeological 
dig in that yard sometime.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:01.880
We seem to be making more 
of a mess, aren't we?

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:06.280
I know!

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.100
Big cleaning?

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:11.900
Hey, Polar Bear.

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:13.360
You're not asking me,

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:16.170
one of the strongest animals 
in the northern hemisphere's ecosystem,

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:19.910
to do big cleaning when I should 
be hibernating, are you?!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.570
You're not very convincing 
when you're dressed like that.

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:24.730
Shut the hell up!

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:26.380
I'm tired, damn it!

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.720
Why am I here, too?

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.300
Cleaning is your hobby, 
right, Mr. Handa?

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.340
Well, I wouldn't call it a hobby...

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.310
My apologies.

00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:39.050
Oh, it's okay. I love cleaning!

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:40.470
Handa!

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:40.470
Yes?

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:43.750
We're gonna do this!

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.720
Handa! Vacuum!

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.810
Y-Yes, sir!

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:05.870
Handa, make sure you get the 
dust in the corners, too.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:06.920
Leave it to me!

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.480
Handa! Don't get the sockets wet!

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.140
Roger!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.170
Mr. Grizzly,

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:29.030
if you use baking soda on the 
spots that don't come off easily,

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.050
that should take care of it.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:31.070
Right!

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:37.030
His work is as violent, 
yet careful, as ever.

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:43.540
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.460
Hello. Oh!

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:50.920
Oh, my.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.880
It's so clean.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.890
Is this good?

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.560
Nothing less from Grizzly.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:08:59.720
See ya.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.380
Oh. Could you wait a moment?

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.200
I'm tired.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.730
Don't freakin' suck me up!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.020
I'm so sorry.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.950
What am I going to do with you?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:17.200
Mr. Grizzly.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:19.430
You're wild!

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.570
Since you're here, 
please have some salmon.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:29.380
Here you go.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:33.030
Salmon hot pot, huh?

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.150
Thank you very much for the salmon.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.930
Oh, it's my pleasure. 
I'm merely sharing our year-end gift.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:40.680
So, I hear you're hibernating?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.290
It's important that you 
get all your nutrients.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.480
Oh, thank you.

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:51.020
Wow! That's good!

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:52.970
Oh, thank goodness.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:56.320
It's some good, fresh, fatty salmon.

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:03.570
Grass after a hard day's work 
is always good, isn't it?

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:06.710
You were just eating grass in the yard!

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.260
Thank you for your hard work.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:11.320
This is something I made.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:13.660
It's a potato and onion padellata.

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:15.650
Thank you.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:20.250
How is it?

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.800
It's delicious, Miss Sasako!

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:24.770
Thank goodness. I feel the same way you do.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.190
It's love, right?

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.650
Um, uh... huh?

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.290
For the potatoes.

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:37.360
Oh, right!

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.170
Thanks for always looking after my son.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:41.930
Not at all.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:43.080
Thank you, as well.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:46.290
That vacuum works very well.

00:10:46.630 --> 00:10:49.470
No kidding. My fur looked like it was burning!

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.020
It's a new model.

00:10:51.510 --> 00:10:54.640
Ours broke, so I was thinking 
of getting a new one.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.300
You can have that one.

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.740
Oh, I didn't mean I wanted it...

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.510
Oh, no. Panda won it 
in the lottery.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:03.540
Oh, really?

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:08.860
I'll give it to you, Mom, as a 
slightly late Christmas present.

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:10.730
Well, thank you.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.190
You're not a bad kid, Panda.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.570
I'm a good kid.

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:17.740
Yes, you are.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:20.530
On the other hand,

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.600
I wish my mom wouldn't clean

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:26.260
since it gets in the way 
of my lazing around.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:33.960
Don't suck me up!

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:39.450
You always say one 
thing too many, Panda.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:45.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:45.280
For Whom Does the Bell Toll?

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:52.670
Good morning.

00:11:53.590 --> 00:11:54.400
It's done.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:11:56.610
What is?

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.110
Welcoming 
Spring

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:06.780
Happy 
New Year!

00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:02.010
Is it a New Year's pine decoration?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:04.170
It's a New Year's tree.

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:06.620
I reused the Christmas tree.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:11.000
I'm guessing it was troublesome 
to put the tree away?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.670
You could say I'm being green.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.540
Something troubling you, 
Mr. Full-Time Panda?

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:27.160
I'm thinking about New Year's vacation.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.530
It's so rough.

00:12:29.530 --> 00:12:32.410
I can't believe we 
only get one week off.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:35.230
You always have five 
days off a week, Panda.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:39.090
Those aren't days off, 
those are fine-tuning days.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:42.690
Pitchers don't pitch every day, right?

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:45.240
What am I going to do?

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.850
If I don't take off at least a month,

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.870
I can't get rid of all 
the fatigue from this year.

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:53.320
I'd like to take that complaint to 
the front of Shinbashi station

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.830
and criticize, protest, and object to it.

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:57.710
Oh?

00:12:57.730 --> 00:13:02.170
Happy New Year

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:00.750
Is this your family, 
Mr. Full-Time Panda?

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.170
Yes, it is.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:05.630
The twin babies are so cute!

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.450
Thanks.

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:13.010
But thinking about going to my 
in-laws' house during vacation

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:14.990
makes me depressed.

00:13:14.990 --> 00:13:16.090
Why's that?

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:19.060
When we went there last year...

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:24.530
I was asked to fix the roof 
because it was leaking.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:28.530
Well, you're good at making models.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.010
But then my mother-in-law 
would complain that

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:34.880
it wasn't done well enough.

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:35.500
Really?

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:37.980
Mr. Full-Time...

00:13:39.330 --> 00:13:41.560
Could you please not 
talk about that here?

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:45.240
Oh, Mr. Handa, perfect timing.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:46.010
What is it?

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.520
Help me write the mailing 
addresses on these New Year's cards.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.310
No, I will not.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:57.910
If your penmanship isn't great, would you 
prefer to do pocket tissue side-job?

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.070
Please do your job properly!

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.610
Well then, have a Happy New Year!

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.610
Close! Too close!

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:09.740
See you next year!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.580
I hope you have a great year!

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:13.990
Open tonight 
to ring in the New Year

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.200
Polar Bear, get me another café mocha.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:18.760
Mr. Penguin,

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:22.230
there's something I want to ask 
you before this year ends.

00:14:22.230 --> 00:14:23.630
And what might that be?

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.090
What's a café mocha?

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:30.430
Is that really something you had 
to ask before the year ends?

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:34.220
When I think about that, 
I can't even sleep at night.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.990
Maybe you should stop napping.

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:40.270
So, what's a café mocha?

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.560
Not giving up, are you?

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:44.910
I don't know that much about it.

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:45.870
What?

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:48.150
You drink it all the time, 
but don't know what it is?

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:50.580
Yeah. Is that wrong?

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:51.160
But...

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.680
Then do you think about

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:56.700
turmeric, coriander, cardamom 
while you eat curry?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.040
Do you think about small dried sardines,

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.370
dried bullet mackerel, 
and Hidaka kelp while eating ramen?

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:04.340
I get it. I'm very sorry.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:08.810
I think you've said something 
like this before, Mr. Penguin.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:10.240
It's déjà vu.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:12.340
In French, it'd be déjà vu.

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.400
Frankly speaking, it just means that

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:18.470
Mr. Penguin hasn't 
grown at all this year.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:21.100
You don't have to speak frankly.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:23.110
Speak frankly <i>(aritei)</i>?

00:15:25.050 --> 00:15:26.500
That would be a holiday <i>(horide—)</i>.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.360
That would be body measuring 
<i>(shintai sokutei)</i>.

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:33.830
That would be apple tea <i>(appuru ti—)</i>.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:37.140
That would be The Secret 
World of Arie—

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:37.700
Ack!

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:40.210
All right, we're done!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:42.810
Don't.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.200
The end of this year would be 
the end for a lot of things.

00:15:45.970 --> 00:15:48.900
More importantly, Polar Bear, 
where's my café mocha?

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.590
Right.

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.330
Here you go.

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:57.990
A drink made by mixing espresso, 
chocolate syrup and steamed milk.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.600
Thank you for your kind explanation.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.030
There aren't any customers.

00:16:10.640 --> 00:16:12.430
Well, it is New Year's Eve.

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.040
I don't mind it.

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.700
It's good to be laid-back at times.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:17.820
True.

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:20.750
How about we hold a 
Red vs. White Pun Telling Contest?

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:23.170
That wouldn't be very laid-back.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:26.780
All right! This is a job for my 
traditional comedic storytelling...

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.840
That can wait until next year.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:29.590
Why?

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:31.980
It's almost midnight,

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:33.340
so we should probably 
eat that one thing...

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.190
Ooh, what?

00:16:35.190 --> 00:16:36.630
You mean soba?

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:41.430
When you think of year-end,

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:45.640
you think of flowing noodles.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.370
Is flowing noodles something you 
do at the end of the year?

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.900
It's like a roller coaster.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:54.360
All right. Here we go!

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:06.210
Cool and delicious.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:11.610
Not bad.

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:12.420
Yeah.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.300
Noodles eaten under the winter sky 
taste especially delicious.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.330
You should have some, too, Miss Sasako.

00:17:19.060 --> 00:17:20.850
I'm a little cold, so...

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:23.250
Then should we make it hot?

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:29.440
It's delicious.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.980
I warmed up the noodles.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:33.460
The soup is great.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.140
This is quite refined.

00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:42.400
This moso bamboo is great, too.

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.520
You're gonna eat that, too, huh?

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:50.090
Polar
 Bear's 
Café

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:52.630
That was great.

00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:56.070
There's not much left of this year.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:57.800
The year went by very fast.

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:02.510
It was in spring when I 
met Panda and Miss Sasako.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:12.150
We had a cherry blossom 
viewing party in spring, too.

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:16.250
Mr. Penguin was pretty drunk.

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:17.540
Was I?

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.120
We went to the beach, too.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.500
Miss Penko!

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:32.670
Mr. Penguin got 
stuck in a watermelon.

00:18:34.270 --> 00:18:36.130
There was a love story, too.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.270
Mr. Penguin totally got dumped.

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:47.890
Could you look for some 
more pleasant memories?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:51.800
I only have unfortunate 
memories of you, Mr. Penguin.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:54.530
That's not true! Right, Miss Sasako?

00:18:55.910 --> 00:18:57.460
Well...

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:04.010
It was hot weeding in the summer,
 but it was a lot of fun.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:09.330
Eating shaved ice in the 
rain was a nice memory, too.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.960
Then there was camping in the mountains,

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.410
and we went to a festival, too.

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.760
We had a ghost story 
telling contest, as well.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:24.940
The sports day and field 
baseball were fun, too.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:29.570
Yeah, those things were fun.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:30.480
See?

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:34.750
I'm glad you lived a life 
without regrets, Mr. Penguin.

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:37.650
Please don't end my life, thanks.

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.890
Let's do lots of fun 
things next year, too.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:42.360
Yes.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.330
All of us.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:45.840
Indeed.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:47.580
Let's enjoy it.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:50.540
Right. All together.

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:51.730
Right?

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:52.460
Yeah!

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:58.880
Good evening.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.670
Welcome!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.720
What brings you here this late?

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:06.900
I was watching TV at home,

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:10.730
but then I felt like drinking 
coffee from Polar Bear's Café.

00:20:11.510 --> 00:20:14.050
I see. I'll pour you some, then.

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:15.120
Also...

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:15.860
Yes?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:20.400
I thought I might run into 
people I know if I came here.

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.320
I'll pour some right 
now, so have a seat.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.290
Good evening!

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:30.190
I'm here!

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:32.810
You, too, Anteater?

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:40.210
Huh?

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.820
Welcome!

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:47.290
Good evening, Mr. Handa.

00:20:47.290 --> 00:20:48.390
Good evening.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:51.640
I didn't think you'd have so 
many customers this evening.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:53.880
I know.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:55.850
I'm surprised, as well.

00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:59.580
Hey, Handa. You came, too?

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:01.050
Yes, just now.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:04.320
Oh? Shouldn't you be 
hibernating, Mr. Grizzly?

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:07.370
Yeah. You should be sleeping.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.840
You woke me up, ya jerk!

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:15.750
Everyone, it's almost midnight.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:18.900
All right! Let's all count down.

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:22.210
Yeah! One... Two...

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:24.050
It's too early still!

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:25.420
Three... Four...

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.810
Or rather, you're counting up!

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:28.460
Five... Six...

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.200
Seven...

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:32.010
New Year's in 33 seconds

00:21:32.010 --> 00:21:32.970
New Year's in 32 seconds

00:21:32.970 --> 00:21:33.220
New Year's in 31 seconds

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:34.940
Thirty more seconds!

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:39.200
29, 28, 27, 26

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:43.050
25, 24, 23, 22...

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:48.740
Good... evening...

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:51.230
H-Hey, you know, you two...

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:54.710
May... this... year...

00:21:55.220 --> 00:21:58.320
You can greet us later!

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:58.320
be... another...

00:21:58.990 --> 00:22:01.130
Please wait!

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:03.510
great... year...

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:03.510
Ack, stop!

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:14.430
Happy...

00:22:14.430 --> 00:22:24.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:24.940
See You Next Year, Too!

00:23:54.950 --> 00:24:24.690
Next Time

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.480
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.480 --> 00:24:00.720
What is it, Panda?

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:02.100
Looking back on this year,

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:05.380
tell us about the thing
 you least want to remember.

00:24:05.380 --> 00:24:06.250
Yeah, no.

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:09.840
What? But I thought I'd use that as 
my background music as I slept.

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:11.100
If that's the case,

00:24:11.100 --> 00:24:12.890
I don't mind saying mine 
if that'll suffice.

00:24:12.890 --> 00:24:14.990
I think it'll be okay if you don't.

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:16.600
Let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.350
In next year's Polar Bear's Café,

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:20.130
we'll do our best with just one picture.

00:24:20.130 --> 00:24:21.110
Let's draw more than one.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:23.300
The Animals' Hidden Talent Competition
New Year's Guest

00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:21.940
Enjoy...

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:23.300
Next year, too!
